course: dictionary
lesson: 496
title: One word, many jobs: ask
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word ask looks simple, but it can do several jobs. Most often it means to say a question so that you get an answer, as in «The teacher asked us to read the first page.» The answer comes after the question.
explain: Ask can also mean to say that you want something. «When something is frustrating, a short break and asking for help work better than giving up.» Here asking for help means politely saying that you need a hand.
explain: Look at the words around ask to find its meaning. In «That's a big ask», the word big tells you it means something hard to expect, like winning every game. Try your meaning in the sentence to check that it fits.
fact: Ask means to say a question so that you get an answer.
fact: Ask also means to say that you want something, as in «ask for help».
fact: Asks, asked and asking are the other forms of ask.
fact: «A big ask» is casual UK and Australian talk for something hard to expect.
fact: In formal writing, people may use «request» or «enquire» where a child would say ask.
exercise: «Any secret someone asks you to keep from your parents is a reason to tell them.» What does asks mean here? | Invites you to a party | Answers a question | Sets a price on something | *Requests, or politely wants you to do something
exercise: «She breaks off a bit of the edge with each hand and asks "And now which is which?"» What is she doing when she asks? | Running away from the table | Stopping to rest | *Saying a question to get an answer | Putting up her hand to speak
exercise: A formal writer might use «request» where a child would say ask. What does request mean? | Sing very loudly | *Ask for something politely | Laugh at someone | Throw something away
test: In «Respect means asking polite questions», what does asking mean? | Saying questions to get answers | Shouting at people | Writing a long letter | *Saying questions to get answers, politely and with kindness
test: Casual talk says «Don't ask» about a story. What does it mean? | *The story is too bad or long to tell | The answer is free | Please ask me again later | You must write the question down
exam: Which formal word could replace ask in «Please ask for a copy»? | *request | swim | giggle | sneeze
